Write an Elixir function `can_construct_ransom_note/2` that takes two string arguments, `ransom_note` and `magazine`, and returns `true` if the ransom note can be formed using letters from the magazine, using each letter at most once, and `false` otherwise. The function should handle empty strings: an empty ransom note can always be constructed. The time complexity should be O(n + m) where n and m are the lengths of the input strings.
